Source: PR #122 CodeRabbit review comment (line 329)

Fix in packages/sdk-core/src/repository/ProfileOperationsImpl.ts update() method

Add check:
if (!existing.success) {
  throw new NetworkError('Profile not found. Use create() for new profiles.');
}

Source: User request to support both blob upload and existing blob ref for profile images.

Example usage after implementation:
```typescript
// Upload new blob (current behavior)
await repo.profile.update({ avatar: new Blob([data], { type: 'image/png' }) });

// Reuse existing blob ref (new capability)
const existingRef = { $type: 'blob', ref: { $link: 'bafyrei...' }, mimeType: 'image/png', size: 1234 };
await repo.profile.update({ avatar: existingRef });
```
